--- !u!114 &49885547
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 49885545}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a1171847eb875841a989d214a1e802a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeTrigger
  dialouge:
    names:
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - Soul #2
    - ...
    - ...
    - Middle Man
    - ...
    - Soul #2
    - ...
    - Soul #2
    - Soul #2
    - ...
    - Soul #2
    - Soul #2
    - ...
    - Soul #2
    - ...
    sentences:
    - 'Then arrives your second defendant, seemingly smaller than the first one you
      notice. '
    - This must be a child. Robbed of their life just as it began.
    - "As they step into the podium, they look around\u2013curious as many children
      often are. Then, looks straight into your eyes."
    - Hi!
    - 'They chirp, catching you off guard. You expect not to be greeted in such a
      friendly manner, let alone so casually. Perhaps the inherent innocence of youth
      has yet to be stripped down from their identity. How fortunate of them to die
      kind. '
    - 'You nod your head in acknowledgement and offer no proper response, instead
      you echo the words you have first spoken to the defendant before this one. '
    - Speak your truth and why you are here, soul of the once living. Tell me your
      faults and reasons, for your conviction may change the line of your fate.
    - The child, seemingly unbothered by your dismissal of greeting, looks deep in
      thought as they fumble with their fingers.
    - "Hm. I think I died because I was hungry\u2026"
    - 'They mumbled, scratching the back of their nape as they continue. '
    - "I guess always feeding my little sister first got to me! But mama did say
      to always treat her first, so I don\u2019t mind."
    - "Well, I mean, it\u2019s also my fault I don\u2019t take enough food really.
      But I just feel bad, ya know? "
    - They sigh, their posture slumped as the weight of their crime slowly weighs
      on their realization.
    - "I guess that\u2019s why I\u2019m here, huh? I just\u2013we didn\u2019t have
      money and my sister needed to eat. I thought I\u2019d be fine not eating myself,
      but my sister\u2026"
    - I wanted to ease a bit of her suffering, even just a little. Even if it meant
      stealing.
    - The child makes a small sound akin to a whimper, damped by their own mouth.
      Their voice then wavers as they mumble their last piece.
    - "I\u2019m sorry. I know it\u2019s bad, mama does too. But we needed to live
      somehow\u2026it was the best chance we got."
    - And the child ends at that, silence returning to the halls with their face
      down. Their once curious eyes now downcast, guilt gnawing at their form and
      therefore refusing to meet your eyes just as bravely as they did before.
