--- !u!114 &248795170
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 248795168}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a1171847eb875841a989d214a1e802a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeTrigger
  dialouge:
    names:
    - ...
    - ...
    - Soul #5
    - ...
    - Middle Man
    - ...
    - Soul #5
    - ...
    - Middle Man
    - Soul #5
    - Soul #5
    - Soul #5
    - ...
    sentences:
    - "The next defendant arrives with a strong air of pride, standing tall and firm
      in a way that demands attention without being overbearing\u2013a feat within
      itself. "
    - 'As they step foot onto the podium, they flash you a smile. Clearly, being
      dead is the most unbothersome thing in their mind. '
    - "Good Mor\u2013! Actually, what time is it here? Nevermind. Good day, Judge!
      I\u2019m here to announce to you that I am by all accounts guilty of whatever
      it is you accuse me of doing! "
    - "\u2026what? "
    - 'Excuse me? '
    - The soul grins, your confusion clearly the cause of their amusement. Nevertheless,
      they continue.
    - "That\u2019s right! I know why I\u2019m here. You\u2019re about to persecute
      me right? Well tell you what, go ahead. Just know that I did it for the sake
      of the people and to expose the truth everyone was owed."
    - 'Interesting. Someone likes getting ahead of themselves. You clear your throat
      and fix your gaze at the brazen soul before you. '
    - Speak your truth and why you are here, soul of the once living. Tell me your
      faults and reasons, for your conviction may change the line of your fate.
    - "Change my fate? Sure is interesting, but alright. For starters, I\u2019m a
      journalist. Rookie one at that, but that didn\u2019t stop me from fighting
      for everything I knew was right."
    - "And in doing so, I\u2019ve violated at least three NDA\u2019s, illegally obtained
      multiple documents that needed clearances I\u2019ll never have, and destroyed
      the data privacy rights of at least six politicians throughout the entire research
      process of my paper. "
    - 'Publishing it was what got me killed, but I have absolutely no regrets. I
      did what I have to do and I will do it again for the greater good of the public. '
    - 'Well that sure is a lot. At least, you suppose, they are aware of their consequences. '
