--- !u!114 &1263837534
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1263837532}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a1171847eb875841a989d214a1e802a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeTrigger
  dialouge:
    names:
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    sentences:
    - The number of defendants has been unending since you began your life as the
      Middle Man.
    - "Quite frankly, it is the sole reason why you exist\u2013one thing you have
      long acknowledged since being put on the pedestal as the perfect and impartial
      Virtue of Court. "
    - Each soul arrives with a story as ridiculous as the last. You have since learned
      that humanity is as unserious as it is unpredictable, oftentimes. It is in
      this way that humanity finds a way to surprise you.
    - "Apart from your amusement towards humanity\u2019s haphazardness, these days,
      you don\u2019t know where you began and where you will end."
    - Was there a you before this? What will come of you once you perish?
    - "To be the Middle Man is your purpose. Humanity\u2019s Hearken, Virtue, and
      Unforgiving One. The one who follows the opinions of the Gods on your shoulders
      and executes humanity\u2019s verdict perfectly."
    - At least, as perfect as things seem. After all, neither Heaven nor Hell have
      descended to express their disappointment at you.
    - Yet.
    - "You follow their rules, rely on the Divine\u2019s preferences, and obediently
      devote yourself to the Divine Masks on your shoulders. Yet, despite everything,
      your future is as uncertain as the souls that stand before you."
    - Inside you is a small, lingering feeling of distress.
    - Doubt seeps in the longer you play your perfect role as judge, jury, and executioner.
    - "You\u2019ve never quite figured out exactly what makes you perfect. It\u2019s
      not something that was spoken, only that perfection means you will not be disgraced."
    - So how long will you be perfect?
    - 'How long will it be until the foundation cracks? '
    - "When will be the first time you\u2019ll make your lasting mistake? "
    - 'At what point, in your borrowed existence, will it be your last? '
    - "If the masks on our shoulders felt your creeping doubt, they speak none of
      it. Much to your chagrin. You\u2019ve relied on every single word they have
      uttered, why is it now that they speak none for your worries?"
    - 'Is it simply because you have done nothing to gravely account for? Even if
      you did, would they notice? '
    - 'Are you the exception to their opinions? Is your final verdict simply to be
      the Middle Man and die as one? '
    - 'Are you that worthless to remain unnoticed by the sole companions you entrust
      your life with?

'
    - "Before you could spiral deeper, the sound of the coffin door opening snaps
      you out of your thoughts. \r\n"
    - Another defendant has arrived.
    - 'Your face, ever-so stoic, cold, and detached remains unchanged as the next
      nervous soul approaches the podium. '
    - At the raise of your hand, you signal the defendant to speak. They flinch at
      the sight of your movement before speaking their testimony, reminding you of
      the long before.
    - 'This was just like your first. How many souls has it been since then, you
      wonder. '
    - Such is another day, another case, and another fate for the Middle Man.
    - As you listen to the testimony of the soul before you, a soft rustle of wind
      catches your ears.
    - A whisper of the wind so soft it easily could have been a delusion. But your
      ears pick up a voice so familiar, so similar to the one that spoke to you from
      the time you first arrived in Sheol with knowing nothing.
    - For a moment, you wonder. Who are they? What are they to Sheol?
    - 'Is there a resident you know not about? '
    - Do the masks know of their existence?
    - 'Curious, you ignore your thoughts for the nth time and tune into the sound
      of the wind. '
    - "Finally, you hear its delicate warning. \r\n"
    - May your obedience never betray you, longest-serving member of the jury.
