--- !u!114 &1637057520
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1637057518}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a1171847eb875841a989d214a1e802a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeTrigger
  dialouge:
    names:
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    sentences:
    - "You are the Jury, Judge and Executioner. The Hearken, the Virtue, the Unforgiving\u2014to
      humanity you are different names, but to the primordial divine, you are the
      Middle Man."
    - In the courtroom of Sheol, you have one task. To send souls to where they belong
      in the divine realm.
    - You will examine the souls of the once living, humans built upon sins and transgressions
      with characters formed from what they believed was right. You decide whether
      they are to suffer for their sins in the raging fire or simmer in the forgiveness
      of the holy water.
    - On your shoulders are the only permanent residences of Sheol. The Weeping Mask
      of Justice sits on your right, whose tears you believe have dampened your right
      shoulder. The Cackling Mask of Judgement sits on your left, vibrating softly
      on your left shoulder from its snickering.
    - The masks are merely pieces of the entities they bear the name of. Pieces of
      which you can only hear from. Their words are absolute and should be considered
      as sacred. For you are their hollow servant, speaking on behalf of their will.
