  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeTrigger
  dialouge:
    names:
    - ...
    - ...
    - ...
    - Middle Man
    - ...
    - Soul #3
    - ...
    - Soul #3
    - Soul #3
    - Soul #3
    - Soul #3
    - ...
    sentences:
    - Then arrives your third defendant with a posture as rigid as a statue. With
      a straight form and their head high, the next soul steps into the podium with
      practiced ease.
    - It seems this one is disciplined enough to hide much of their discomfort.
    - "They stand silently still, seemingly unwilling to speak before you\u2013perhaps
      a small telltale of nervousness. As such, you say your line as a greeting. "
    - Speak your truth and why you are here, soul of the once living. Tell me your
      faults and reasons, for your conviction may change the line of your fate.
    - The soul nods before clearing their throat. With a voice clear and soft, they
      respond.
    - "I dedicated my life for my duty as a private nurse for a very\u2026 important
      individual. "
    - "Suddenly hesitant to continue, they pause for a moment before gaining their
      resolve\u2013as if pushing down their feelings for the truth of the matter."
    - A politician. I served a politician of my country that was far from a good
      man. By all means, it is my regret that I treated such a vile man of cruel
      repertoire.
    - "To have sustained a life that harmed many and killed plenty\u2026I regret
      most of my life because of my duty. A duty that required me to practice compassion
      and respect for the inherent dignity of every person, even criminals."
    - Which means, regardless of my ethical values, a nurse's primary commitment
      is the patient. Especially a patient so powerful, protected, and promises a
      hefty paycheck.
    - "By all means, I know I have done nothing wrong. But\u2026 it also meant that
      I helped keep that putrid man alive and I\u2026\r\n"
    - Defeated, the soul resorts to silence. This must be a matter that has long
      since weighed their conscience.  It seems that this is all they are willing
      to speak about the matter.
